9587","id":4500887584,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDEYYIA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T17:26:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T17:26:53Z","body":"> Is that because there are checks elsewhere?\r\n\r\nI assume so since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118629 was merged.\r\n\r\nBy the way, I noticed https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110119 is still open, but I think it's superseded by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118629.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500887584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501420765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-4501420765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":4501420765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDE463Q","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T18:28:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T18:28:00Z","body":"> > Is that because there are checks elsewhere?\r\n> \r\n> I assume so since #118629 was merged.\r\n\r\nCan you double check? I don't love the idea of setting the mode despite knowing it won't work. If we are going to leave the code as-is we need to be confident that it doesn't cause side effects","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501420765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501706309","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-4501706309","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":4501706309,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDFKWRQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T19:03:53Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T19:11:13Z","body":"> Can you double check?\r\n\r\nThe code added by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118629 ensures we use bilinear scaling in Mobile/Compatibility, but it still reconfigures 3D buffers even if it doesn't need to, so I think it's better to use early returns.\r\n\r\nI've added early returns to `viewport_set_scaling_3d_mode()`. While doing this, I noticed all the warning prints and early returns are behind `#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED`. To get consistent behavior between debug and release builds, we'd need to remove this `#ifdef`.\r\n\r\nShould we remove the `#ifdef` entirely or keep the warning messages behind them (but move the `return`s outside)? Personally, I would prefer to keep warnings in release mode (they won't be visible to the player unless running from a terminal anyway).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501706309/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4503501757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-4503501757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":4503501757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDG37vQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T23:34:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T23:34:21Z","body":"> I've added early returns to viewport_set_scaling_3d_mode(). While doing this, I noticed all the warning prints and early returns are behind #ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED. To get consistent behavior between debug and release builds, we'd need to remove this #ifdef.\r\n> \r\n> Should we remove the #ifdef entirely or keep the warning messages behind them (but move the returns outside)? Personally, I would prefer to keep warnings in release mode (they won't be visible to the player unless running from a terminal anyway).\r\n\r\nWere there any reported issues from this in earlier versions? Remember, these returned before https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111806. If no one ran into an issue I wouldn't worry about it. Just restore the behaviour from before it regressed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111806","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4503501757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4503989519","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-4503989519","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":4503989519,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDHVtDw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T01:30:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T01:39:22Z","body":"> Were there any reported issues from this in earlier versions?\r\n\r\nNot that I know of. As I mentioned, changing 3D scaling to FSR2/MetalFX Temporal when unsupported didn't cause jittering to occur since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118629 was merged to fix that particular issue.\r\n\r\nI removed the instances of `#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED` in `renderer_viewport.cpp` to make it behave like before https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111806 (which didn't have any `#ifdef`s in that file beforehand). It should now follow the same flow as before, except warnings are printed instead of errors. I've tested this on both editor and release export templates with the MRP from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119487#issuecomment-4493185503.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4503989519/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4535685556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-4535685556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":4535685556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDlkRtA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T16:23:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T16:23:33Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4535685556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4695448105","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-4695448105","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":4695448105,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF97aKQ","user":{"login":"mechalynx","id":8427257,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0MjcyNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8427257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx","html_url":"https://github.com/mechalynx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mechalynx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-12T21:03:45Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T23:00:56Z","body":"> By the way, I noticed #110119 is still open, but I think it's superseded by #118629.\r\n\r\n#110119 is not superseded by #118629, it fixes a different issue. #110119 had the same jitter fix for the cases fixed by #110672 and, since that PR was merged first, the subsequent rebase removed that part of #110119.\r\n\r\n#110119 is meant to fix a subviewport render thread crash in the case of it becoming too small for FSR2 and applies an upper limit to viewport size so it can't exceed device limits. The similarity is in using the same fix for jitter after bilinear fallback, which in #110119 is due to viewport size, hence the confusion.\r\n\r\n(I know this is closed but it's where the comment was made and I hadn't seen it earlier)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4695448105/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5956077241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119587#issuecomment-5956077241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119587","id":5956077241,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYwKGuQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T15:52:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T15:52:06Z","body":"Cherry-picked for 4.6.4.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5956077241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]